  "selection": "One three-edge chain and two selection methods. The first method is a polarity pair: multiply by 3 on edge (0,1) when edge (1,2) is present, and the same multiply when that edge is absent. The present cell is the atlas-010 three-edge multiply. It is the matched partner, not a new table. The second method is a length-2 pair at factor 3, action either, polarity present. One list puts two guards on (0,1). The other list puts one guard on (0,1) and one guard on (2,3), both conditioned on (1,2). The two single constraints used by those lists are stored. The atlas-009 factor-2 path grid is not this list. The atlas-005 modular menu is not this list. Not scheduled to explain the atlas-009 marginals, the atlas-010 defects, the atlas-011 defects, PAT-012, or PAT-014. A comparison of a polarity cell with a length-2 cell changes cardinality and arrangement together. It is joint. Formation and dissolution are not in the round. ATLAS-Q04 stays out.",
